Gabo!

239
00:10:37,733 --> 00:10:38,733
[RUDY] Gabo!

240
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:41,700
Hey, Gabo!

241
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:45,367
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

242
00:10:45,367 --> 00:10:46,333
Gabo!

243
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:49,967
- What's your problem?!
- [BETCHAY] Rudy!

244
00:10:49,967 --> 00:10:51,433
[RUDY] Gabo!

245
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:53,167
Didn't we just talk about this?!

246
00:10:53,833 --> 00:10:58,200
You promised you'd change
for the better!

247
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,933
But that animal's gone too far!

248
00:11:00,933 --> 00:11:03,233
I just got out of jail
and he's already provoking me!

249
00:11:03,233 --> 00:11:05,267
He's the reason I was jailed
in the first place!

250
00:11:05,267 --> 00:11:06,500
Well, too bad for him!

251
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:11,167
Now everyone knows who's boss
here in Ginintuang Lupa!

252
00:11:11,967 --> 00:11:13,400
- Yeah.
- He's right.

253
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:14,833
[DANTE] Gabo.

254
00:11:14,833 --> 00:11:17,333
You really can't control
your anger, can you?

255
00:11:17,333 --> 00:11:20,267
What if Paquito
gets back at you?

256
00:11:20,267 --> 00:11:22,533
[IPE] Oh, I don't think so.

257
00:11:22,533 --> 00:11:25,000
Gabo crushed all his enemies.

258
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,733
[BONG] You saw, didn't you?

259
00:11:26,733 --> 00:11:31,133
He beat all of them to a pulp.
I doubt they'd want another go.

260
00:11:31,133 --> 00:11:34,200
They're probably too embarrassed
to show up here again.

261
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:37,467
I'm sure after this, no one will
follow them out of fear again.

262
00:11:37,467 --> 00:11:39,267
- Yeah!
- That's right!

263
00:11:39,267 --> 00:11:42,733
That's where you're wrong.
I know Paquito.

264
00:11:42,767 --> 00:11:46,033
He'll just find another way
to torment us again.

265
00:11:46,033 --> 00:11:48,167
Let them try, Miss Mameng!

266
00:11:48,167 --> 00:11:50,300
They'll get more than a beating
from Gabo.

267
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:51,333
[DIDAY] Gabo!

268
00:11:51,333 --> 00:11:53,400
If Django and Paquito
return here for revenge,

269
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,300
we'll back you up!

270
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:57,300
- Right, everyone?!
- [WEAKLY] Y-Yes.

271
00:11:57,300 --> 00:12:00,167
Louder!
Or I'll hit you in the face!

272
00:12:00,167 --> 00:12:01,367
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

273
00:12:01,367 --> 00:12:03,067
- We got your back!
- You can count on us!

274
00:12:03,067 --> 00:12:04,200
[RUDY] Gabo.

275
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:07,367
It's only your first day
out of jail,

276
00:12:07,367 --> 00:12:09,467
but you already put
our family at risk!

277
00:12:09,467 --> 00:12:12,767
Now, we'll have to live
in constant fear,

278
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:14,967
dreading the day Paquito's group
returns for payback.

279
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:15,967
Just let them try!

280
00:12:17,067 --> 00:12:19,033
If they lay a finger on you,

281
00:12:19,033 --> 00:12:21,633
I'll fight back even if it means
ending up in jail again!

282
00:12:21,633 --> 00:12:28,600
[MUSIC TURNS MOROSE]

283
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:35,667
What are you looking at,
you nosybodies?!

284
00:12:35,667 --> 00:12:39,200
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

285
00:12:40,267 --> 00:12:43,767
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [PUNCHING BAG CHAINS RATTLE]

286
00:12:43,767 --> 00:12:48,600
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

287
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:52,567
[BETCHAY]
What did I tell you?

288
00:12:52,567 --> 00:12:54,900
He hasn't changed at all.

289
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,500
Come on, Rudy.

290
00:12:57,500 --> 00:13:02,200
He's been getting into fights
ever since he was a kid.

291
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:05,167
He's been into all kinds
of trouble!

292
00:13:05,167 --> 00:13:07,200
[MAMENG]
Hey, watch your mouth.

293
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:10,033
What did Gabo ever do to you?

294
00:13:10,033 --> 00:13:12,067
Why do you always think
the worst of him?

295
00:13:12,067 --> 00:13:15,100
Is it because he's not
your real son?

296
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:17,667
- Wait a minute--
- Is that why...

297
00:13:17,667 --> 00:13:19,333
...you never gave him
your support?

298
00:13:19,333 --> 00:13:23,933
Hey! How dare you say
I never supported that kid?!

299
00:13:23,967 --> 00:13:26,100
I raised him!

300
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:28,467
I stood up as his mother!

301
00:13:28,467 --> 00:13:31,433
I'm just saying the truth
because I know him.

302
00:13:31,433 --> 00:13:33,900
I know Gabo damn well!

303
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:35,433
- That's enough now,
- So you have no right...

304
00:13:35,433 --> 00:13:38,100
- ...to question me!
- Miss Betchay, that's enough.

305
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:42,267
We all know the truth, okay?
We know Gabo is a good guy.

306
00:13:42,267 --> 00:13:45,900
Unless he's provoked, of course.
Because then he'd retaliate.

307
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:48,000
- I didn't--
- Enough! That's enough!

308
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:50,867
Enough.

309
00:13:50,867 --> 00:13:52,300
I'll talk to Gabo.

310
00:13:53,667 --> 00:13:57,433
I haven't given up hope
that he'll change.

311
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:02,533
Just let me talk to him.

312
00:14:02,533 --> 00:14:03,667
[BETCHA] Rudy!

313
00:14:06,033 --> 00:14:10,600
- This is all your fault.
- Why me? You started this.

314
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,800
- Me?
- Enough.

315
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:14,567
- You're spewing nonsense!
- I'm just saying the truth!

316
00:14:14,567 --> 00:14:17,233
- Okay, that's enough! Enough!
- Calm down. Stop it!

317
00:14:17,233 --> 00:14:18,333
[RUDY] Gabo.

318
00:14:19,767 --> 00:14:20,867
Why did you do that?!

319
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:23,733
Tell me!

320
00:14:23,733 --> 00:14:26,967
You promised you'd change
for the better, didn't you?!

321
00:14:26,967 --> 00:14:28,467
What if something bad
had happened to you?!

322
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:30,067
What if they killed you?!

323
00:14:30,067 --> 00:14:31,433
But they've gone too far, Pa!

324
00:14:33,067 --> 00:14:34,667
Django has gone too far!

325
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:43,767
Ever since I was a kid...

326
00:14:47,833 --> 00:14:49,833
he has always picked on me.

327
00:14:52,333 --> 00:14:54,367
He has been tormenting me.

328
00:14:56,667 --> 00:14:59,100
He's the reason I was imprisoned
for eight years!

329
00:15:00,267 --> 00:15:02,133
So, while I was behind bars,

330
00:15:02,167 --> 00:15:05,600
I promised myself
that when I get out,

331
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:09,900
I'll make him feel all
the suffering I went through!

332
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:15,500
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:16,633
Son...

334
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,833
Don't waste your life.

335
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,067
You're still young.

336
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:28,733
Don't waste your time

337
00:15:28,733 --> 00:15:31,033
getting revenge from
those good-for-nothing pricks!

338
00:15:32,133 --> 00:15:35,900
I have so many dreams for you.

339
00:15:35,933 --> 00:15:39,833
But most of all, I just want you
to have a good life.

340
00:15:39,833 --> 00:15:41,233
That's all I want.

341
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:46,233
Son, I'm your father.

342
00:15:48,733 --> 00:15:52,133
[SNIFFLES] Do you love me
as your father?

343
00:15:59,567 --> 00:16:00,900
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

344
00:16:02,367 --> 00:16:04,200
I love you, Pa.

345
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:08,500
Please forgive me.

346
00:16:12,133 --> 00:16:14,167
I'm sorry I got carried away.

347
00:16:18,333 --> 00:16:19,367
Son...

348
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:22,833
if you really love me,

349
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:26,733
please listen
to what I'm telling you.

350
00:16:29,033 --> 00:16:32,933
I just want you to live
a decent life.

351
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:35,767
I... I just want you...

352
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,167
to have a good family.

353
00:16:38,967 --> 00:16:40,900
I want you to have
a better future.

354
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:44,800
To get you out of this place.

355
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:49,933
[RUDY SOBBING SOFTLY]

356
00:16:53,167 --> 00:16:54,967
I understand you.

357
00:16:56,067 --> 00:16:57,867
Please forgive me
for what I did earlier.

358
00:17:00,033 --> 00:17:02,633
For letting my emotions
get the best of me.

359
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:10,333
And for what I did to Django.

360
00:17:12,233 --> 00:17:14,033
Son, if you love me...

361
00:17:15,133 --> 00:17:18,000
please take my words to heart.

362
00:17:22,367 --> 00:17:27,200
I won't make you do anything
that will ruin your life.

363
00:17:28,033 --> 00:17:29,667
Now that you're free...

364
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:35,833
please don't go back
to your old ways.

365
00:17:38,233 --> 00:17:39,433
Pa...

366
00:17:42,667 --> 00:17:44,433
I love you very much.

367
00:17:45,567 --> 00:17:47,700
And I have so much
respect for you.

368
00:17:48,867 --> 00:17:50,833
I promise you...

369
00:17:52,467 --> 00:17:54,067
that starting tomorrow...

370
00:17:56,033 --> 00:17:57,967
I'll try my best to change.

371
00:17:59,933 --> 00:18:01,933
I'll look for a job.

372
00:18:02,867 --> 00:18:05,567
And I'll avoid getting
into any trouble.

373
00:18:06,867 --> 00:18:10,700
[RUDY SNIFFLING]

374
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:13,167
Thank you, son.

375
00:18:13,167 --> 00:18:15,933
- Thank you.
- I'm sorry, Pa.

376
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:20,300
- [RUDY SNIFFLES]
- Please forgive me.

377
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:27,200
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

378
00:18:28,933 --> 00:18:31,133
Update me on the surveillance
in Chinatown, okay?

379
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:33,433
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

380
00:18:33,433 --> 00:18:34,733
Alright, I'll get going.

381
00:18:35,067 --> 00:18:36,600
- I'll come along.
- Come on.

382
00:18:37,867 --> 00:18:40,133
Uh... Sam, Sam! Hold on.

383
00:18:40,133 --> 00:18:41,500
You left something.

384
00:18:43,167 --> 00:18:44,167
Here.

385
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:46,100
You left these.

386
00:18:47,467 --> 00:18:50,133
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:18:50,133 --> 00:18:51,867
You forgot these.

388
00:18:52,633 --> 00:18:55,767
That's for the most beautiful
woman here in NCIA.

389
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:57,967
Not for her desk.

390
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:01,867
Oh, are you headed home?

391
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:04,667
Let me escort you so I know
you'll get home safely.

392
00:19:04,667 --> 00:19:06,333
No need. I can protect myself.

393
00:19:06,533 --> 00:19:07,500
Is that so?

394
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:08,567
Just text me then.

395
00:19:11,333 --> 00:19:12,633
Bye.

396
00:19:15,133 --> 00:19:16,200
Take care, Sam.

397
00:19:16,967 --> 00:19:18,533
Put those in a vase.
They're pretty.

398
00:19:18,533 --> 00:19:25,433
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:19:27,767 --> 00:19:28,767
[KAREN EXHALES]

400
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:31,467
Your future boyfriend
is so sweet.

401
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:33,600
Excuse me.
He's not my future boyfriend.

402
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:34,933
Why not?

403
00:19:36,633 --> 00:19:38,267
Did you see
how he acted earlier?

404
00:19:38,667 --> 00:19:41,533
He acts as if
we're in a relationship.

405
00:19:41,933 --> 00:19:43,533
He even wanted me to text him.

406
00:19:44,133 --> 00:19:45,367
[SCOFFS] Who the hell is he?

407
00:19:45,667 --> 00:19:46,700
He's Sir Sebastian.

408
00:19:47,167 --> 00:19:48,167
The one.

409
00:19:48,167 --> 00:19:49,900
Whatever. I'm going home.

410
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,500
Karen! Karen! Hold on.

411
00:19:58,633 --> 00:20:01,033
Do you think Sir Seb
has a chance with Ma'am Sam?

412
00:20:01,667 --> 00:20:02,833
That's the thing.

413
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,200
Looks like her heart
needs to defrost for a while.

414
00:20:05,967 --> 00:20:07,333
Well then, we'll make it work.

415
00:20:07,533 --> 00:20:09,200
I know they'll end up together.

416
00:20:09,900 --> 00:20:11,700
- True.
- But if they can't be together

417
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:12,700
then...

418
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,167
I think we can be together.

419
00:20:14,167 --> 00:20:15,467
Ugh!

420
00:20:15,467 --> 00:20:16,700
Don't say that again.

421
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:19,267
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

422
00:20:19,267 --> 00:20:20,200
Such nonsense.

423
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:24,000
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

424
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,167
[MUSIC FADES]

425
00:20:27,667 --> 00:20:29,300
He's so full of himself.

426
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,267
He just came back...

427
00:20:33,567 --> 00:20:35,367
and he thinks
he runs Ginintuang Lupa.

428
00:20:36,333 --> 00:20:37,567
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

429
00:20:37,567 --> 00:20:38,800
What's your plan, Django?

430
00:20:39,633 --> 00:20:41,033
I'll let him enjoy his win
right now.

431
00:20:42,233 --> 00:20:43,933
[CHUCKLES EVILLY]

432
00:20:49,167 --> 00:20:50,800
But when the time comes,

433
00:20:53,333 --> 00:20:54,667
I'll make sure...

434
00:20:57,067 --> 00:20:58,367
he never gets up.

435
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:01,333
You're right, boss.
We have to make Gabo pay.

436
00:21:02,133 --> 00:21:04,500
Sooner or later, boss,
we have to make him pay.

437
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,533
[TOLITS]
You guys know Django well.

438
00:21:10,767 --> 00:21:12,933
- He doesn't accept defeat.
- Take a shot, man!

439
00:21:12,933 --> 00:21:14,467
He'll sure get back at Gabo.

440
00:21:15,367 --> 00:21:18,233
The problem will get worse
if this reaches Paquito.

441
00:21:18,233 --> 00:21:20,533
Those two will make Gabo's life
a living hell

442
00:21:20,767 --> 00:21:22,100
until they get even.

443
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:23,667
Not only to Gabo.

444
00:21:23,667 --> 00:21:26,667
The whole Ginintuang Lupa will
be in chaos if that happens.

445
00:21:27,067 --> 00:21:28,333
Hold, on, hold on, hold on.

446
00:21:28,333 --> 00:21:29,233
Ouch!

447
00:21:29,233 --> 00:21:30,367
- Sorry, sorry.
- What is it?

448
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,333
What if...

449
00:21:32,967 --> 00:21:34,300
we just abandon the group?

450
00:21:35,667 --> 00:21:37,800
I don't want to work
for that father and son anymore.

451
00:21:38,300 --> 00:21:39,333
What do you think?

452
00:21:39,533 --> 00:21:41,333
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

453
00:21:41,867 --> 00:21:42,800
You're right.

454
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,600
Let's dip out.

455
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:48,833
- We'll start a new group.
- [EXCLAIMS]

456
00:21:49,033 --> 00:21:50,000
Shhh!

457
00:21:50,433 --> 00:21:52,433
So we won't have any cuts
from our earnings.

458
00:21:52,767 --> 00:21:56,433
We won't have to give anything
to Paquito and Django.

459
00:21:56,667 --> 00:21:58,733
- Right? Right?
- That's true! That's true!

460
00:21:59,467 --> 00:22:01,533
Hold on, hold on. If we dip out,

461
00:22:02,067 --> 00:22:04,133
Django and Paquito
might get back at us.

462
00:22:04,433 --> 00:22:05,833
You're a coward, aren't you
Are you a coward?

463
00:22:06,233 --> 00:22:07,200
Then...

464
00:22:08,633 --> 00:22:10,333
- We'll befriend Gabo.
- Oh, yes.

465
00:22:10,867 --> 00:22:12,633
- Huh?
- If we're friends with Gabo,

466
00:22:12,833 --> 00:22:14,833
for sure, we'll have protection.

467
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:16,267
- Yes.
- You saw what happened earlier.

468
00:22:16,300 --> 00:22:18,467
- Yes.
- Gabo knocked out Django.

469
00:22:18,467 --> 00:22:20,167
- Yes.
- You saw it. You too.

470
00:22:20,167 --> 00:22:22,933
You saw it, right?
That's what I'm saying.

471
00:22:22,933 --> 00:22:27,367
If we side with Gabo,
we'll get caught in their fight.

472
00:22:27,367 --> 00:22:29,767
You backing down already, huh?
Are you that unsure?

473
00:22:29,767 --> 00:22:31,300
What's your problem, huh?

474
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:35,600
No matter what we do,
those two will clash again.

475
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:40,800
What matters is backing
whoever's got the upper hand.

476
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:45,867
- And we just saw Gabo!
- Oh!

477
00:22:45,867 --> 00:22:47,867
- Gabo! You get it now?
- Exactly.

478
00:22:47,867 --> 00:22:49,233
So do we have a plan?

479
00:22:49,267 --> 00:22:51,000
- Alright? Our plan's set.
- I'm good with it.

480
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,933
- Gabo.
- You can handle this, yeah?

481
00:22:52,933 --> 00:22:55,000
- Suit yourselves.
- Come on, let's go.

482
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,767
We're with Gabo,
he's the strong one.

483
00:22:56,767 --> 00:22:58,767
You saw what happened
to Django, right?

484
00:22:58,767 --> 00:22:59,933
Turns out he's all bark,
no bite.

485
00:22:59,933 --> 00:23:04,333
[CAR ENGINE REVVING]

486
00:23:08,833 --> 00:23:11,167
- Good evening, ma'am!
- Good evening.

487
00:23:11,167 --> 00:23:13,100
Thank you.

488
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:15,967
Mac, open the big gate,
will you?

489
00:23:15,967 --> 00:23:18,200
- It's risky bringing out the...
- [KNOCKING ON DOOR]

490
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:21,867
Sam?

491
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:24,433
- Sam. Dear.
- Mom.

492
00:23:24,433 --> 00:23:26,467
What happened to you?
Did you get hurt?

493
00:23:26,467 --> 00:23:29,200
- No. I'm okay, Mom.
- Huh? Are you sure?

494
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:31,767
Wow,
you were incredible out there!

495
00:23:31,767 --> 00:23:33,433
And your mom and I
watched the whole thing!

496
00:23:33,433 --> 00:23:35,367
Honestly, it was so impressive!

497
00:23:35,367 --> 00:23:37,100
You've really got
something special, ma'am!

498
00:23:37,100 --> 00:23:40,300
- [ISOBEL] Exactly.
- Go! Go, Sam! You were amazing!

499
00:23:40,300 --> 00:23:41,833
You really are something else.

500
00:23:41,833 --> 00:23:44,900
I know she's always good
at doing her job,

501
00:23:44,900 --> 00:23:46,933
so I never doubted
you'd be safe.

502
00:23:46,933 --> 00:23:48,467
Hmm!

503
00:23:48,467 --> 00:23:51,367
- Dear, where did these...
- Ay, oo nga! Oh my gosh!

504
00:23:51,367 --> 00:23:53,200
...beautiful flowers come from?

505
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:55,733
- They're so heavy.
- They're from Sebastian.

506
00:23:55,767 --> 00:23:58,733
The guy who's been
courting you forever?

507
00:23:58,733 --> 00:24:01,033
Look at that. So sweet!

508
00:24:02,467 --> 00:24:04,300
So, are you finally
going to say yes?

509
00:24:05,267 --> 00:24:08,133
Mom, I'm not thinking
about that right now.

510
00:24:08,133 --> 00:24:09,367
Oh, is that so?

511
00:24:09,367 --> 00:24:12,167
Yes, Mom.
That's not our priority.

512
00:24:12,167 --> 00:24:14,867
Our careers come first.

513
00:24:14,867 --> 00:24:17,000
In fact, here's the proof.

514
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:19,200
You brought work home.

515
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:20,233
No.

516
00:24:20,233 --> 00:24:22,233
There's an explanation for this.

517
00:24:22,233 --> 00:24:25,067
I need to finish
our investigation.

518
00:24:25,067 --> 00:24:27,433
Sir Delgado just
made me team leader.

519
00:24:27,433 --> 00:24:28,600
Really?!

520
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:31,700
- Mm! [CHUCKLES]
- I'm so proud of you, dear.

521
00:24:31,733 --> 00:24:34,700
Your dad would be too.

522
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:36,400
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

523
00:24:37,467 --> 00:24:38,967
Speaking of your dad,

524
00:24:38,967 --> 00:24:42,133
he has something
important to tell both of you.

525
00:24:42,133 --> 00:24:44,833
That's why Aunt Pinky's here.

526
00:24:44,833 --> 00:24:46,267
- Let's go.
- Come on.

527
00:24:46,267 --> 00:24:48,333
- Man, I'm dying of thirst.
- Okay.

528
00:24:48,333 --> 00:24:49,467
Come on, hurry.

529
00:24:49,467 --> 00:24:53,033
- Okay, Pinky, look who's here.
- Oh, hi!

530
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:54,233
Hello!

531
00:24:54,233 --> 00:24:57,400
- Go say hi.
- Oh, hello! [SMOOCHES]

532
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:59,100
Hi, Aunt Pinky!

533
00:24:59,100 --> 00:25:01,500
- I missed you.
- It's nice you could stop by.

534
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:02,600
Yes!

535
00:25:03,900 --> 00:25:05,200
What's up?

536
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:10,033
Well, your Aunt Pinky has this
piece of property she's selling.

537
00:25:10,033 --> 00:25:13,267
Your mom and I thought it was
a great business opportunity,

538
00:25:13,267 --> 00:25:15,400
so we bought it.

539
00:25:16,467 --> 00:25:20,400
With the economy so unstable,
high oil prices,

540
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:22,967
conflicts everywhere,
and endless corruption

541
00:25:22,967 --> 00:25:24,967
here in the Philippines,

542
00:25:24,967 --> 00:25:27,267
the previous owner
decided to move abroad.

543
00:25:27,267 --> 00:25:30,500
So we got the land
for a really low price.

544
00:25:31,700 --> 00:25:35,300
- Where's this property located?
- In Ginintuang Lupa.

545
00:25:35,300 --> 00:25:38,900
Investors are already
interested.

546
00:25:38,933 --> 00:25:40,567
They would like to see the
property next week.

547
00:25:40,767 --> 00:25:43,267
Yes, it's a very,
very good location.

548
00:25:43,267 --> 00:25:48,500
The mayor has big plans
for that area.

549
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:51,933
And Isobel, if this goes
through? We'll be
sitting on a goldmine.

550
00:25:51,933 --> 00:25:53,833
Yes.

551
00:25:53,833 --> 00:25:56,033
Wait a second, Ginintuang Lupa?

552
00:25:56,033 --> 00:25:57,567
But there are so many families
living there.

553
00:25:57,567 --> 00:25:59,800
And that area's known for crime.

554
00:25:59,800 --> 00:26:01,967
There's nothing
to worry about, Sam.

555
00:26:01,967 --> 00:26:04,133
The court already
ordered them to leave.

556
00:26:04,133 --> 00:26:06,500
They should've been gone
ages ago.

557
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:08,533
But Max,
where are they supposed to go?

558
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:10,267
Sam.

559
00:26:10,267 --> 00:26:13,067
Don't worry about
where they'll end up.

560
00:26:13,067 --> 00:26:15,500
They'll just move
to the hills or somewhere.

561
00:26:15,500 --> 00:26:17,367
They always find
a place to stay.

562
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:19,733
They're used to fending
for themselves.

563
00:26:19,733 --> 00:26:22,133
But, Mom, we can't just
let them be.

564
00:26:22,133 --> 00:26:24,000
Many families
will be left homeless.

565
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:25,633
Let's put it this way.

566
00:26:25,633 --> 00:26:28,467
They've been staying at
Ginintuang Lupa for years.

567
00:26:28,467 --> 00:26:31,433
So, as the new owners,

568
00:26:31,433 --> 00:26:34,933
it's our turn to make use
of that property. Okay?

569
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:37,733
That's my decision
and that's final.

570
00:26:40,067 --> 00:26:42,467
Okay.
So, have you signed it?

571
00:26:42,500 --> 00:26:43,967
- Yes, I did.
- It's all done?

572
00:26:43,967 --> 00:26:48,067
Oh, there's something
I'd like to discuss with you.

573
00:26:48,067 --> 00:26:49,167
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

574
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:52,633
- Knock, knock.
- Oh. Hi.

575
00:26:52,633 --> 00:26:54,167
How's my team leader?

576
00:26:55,567 --> 00:26:56,600
Hmm?

577
00:26:56,600 --> 00:26:58,100
Well...

578
00:26:58,900 --> 00:27:01,867
I brought you some coffee
to boost your energy.

579
00:27:01,867 --> 00:27:04,267
- Thank you.
- I'm going to bed too.

580
00:27:04,267 --> 00:27:06,167
- Alright.
- Max.

581
00:27:06,900 --> 00:27:09,100
I want to ask you something.

582
00:27:09,100 --> 00:27:10,100
What?

583
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:15,033
Do you really agree
with Daddy's decision?

584
00:27:16,367 --> 00:27:17,900
Well...

585
00:27:17,900 --> 00:27:19,467
Yeah.

586
00:27:19,467 --> 00:27:21,433
That's a good investment.

587
00:27:21,433 --> 00:27:22,700
Don't you think?

588
00:27:23,733 --> 00:27:27,500
I'm just worried about those
people who'll lose their homes.

589
00:27:27,500 --> 00:27:28,967
There are many
families there.

590
00:27:28,967 --> 00:27:32,533
Shouldn't we protect them
as enforcers of the law?

591
00:27:32,533 --> 00:27:34,267
No. No, Sam.

592
00:27:34,267 --> 00:27:37,533
Remember, they are
illegal settlers.

593
00:27:37,533 --> 00:27:40,767
It is our
job to enforce the law.

594
00:27:40,767 --> 00:27:41,800
Okay?

595
00:27:43,367 --> 00:27:46,367
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

596
00:27:46,367 --> 00:27:49,067
I wonder what RJ would
say about all of this.

597
00:27:49,967 --> 00:27:51,067
What would he say?

598
00:27:52,267 --> 00:27:55,633
He'd always agree to what
Daddy says.

599
00:27:55,633 --> 00:27:58,000
He'd go, "Yes, okay."

600
00:27:59,800 --> 00:28:01,833
Enough of the drama, okay?

601
00:28:01,833 --> 00:28:04,400
Stop thinking negative thoughts.

602
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:05,467
I mean, come on.

603
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:09,500
Look at your achievements.
You're a team leader,

604
00:28:09,500 --> 00:28:12,333
and you were a hero
during that bus incident.

605
00:28:12,333 --> 00:28:14,033
Oh come on, Max.

606
00:28:14,033 --> 00:28:17,333
Don't mention that bus
incident again.

607
00:28:17,333 --> 00:28:19,033
It's making my blood boil.

608
00:28:19,033 --> 00:28:21,533
Why? What happened?

609
00:28:22,267 --> 00:28:24,433
A guy took advantage
of me.

610
00:28:24,433 --> 00:28:25,733
What?!

611
00:28:27,033 --> 00:28:28,633
What exactly did he do?

612
00:28:28,633 --> 00:28:30,033
He kissed me.

613
00:28:30,033 --> 00:28:33,100
He kissed you?! Does he know
that's harassment?

614
00:28:33,100 --> 00:28:34,367
I'll file charges
against him.

615
00:28:34,367 --> 00:28:36,133
I'll arrest him myself.

616
00:28:36,133 --> 00:28:37,233
Where is he?

617
00:28:37,233 --> 00:28:39,233
I don't even know
his name.

618
00:28:39,233 --> 00:28:41,233
What does he look like?
Describe him to me.

619
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:52,333
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

620
00:28:58,467 --> 00:29:00,167
Why are you smiling?

621
00:29:02,233 --> 00:29:04,333
- I was smiling?
- Yes.

622
00:29:04,333 --> 00:29:06,867
What are you talking about?
I wasn't smiling.

623
00:29:06,867 --> 00:29:07,933
Yes, I saw it.

624
00:29:07,933 --> 00:29:11,133
What? That's gross.
Why would I smile?

625
00:29:11,133 --> 00:29:15,100
Did you find what he did
offensive?

626
00:29:15,100 --> 00:29:16,567
Yes, of course.

627
00:29:16,567 --> 00:29:19,633
Besides, if you've seen
what he looks like,

628
00:29:19,633 --> 00:29:21,767
you'll see that he's
gross and filthy.

629
00:29:21,767 --> 00:29:23,767
He looks unkempt and in
need of a shower.

630
00:29:23,767 --> 00:29:26,667
Plus, his hair looks dry.

631
00:29:26,667 --> 00:29:29,967
And no one in their right mind
would pretend to faint

632
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,600
and kiss a stranger.

633
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:34,900
No decent guy would do that
unless he's a pervert.

634
00:29:34,900 --> 00:29:38,433
That was such a long answer
for one question.

635
00:29:42,433 --> 00:29:45,667
I thought you were going
to bed.

636
00:29:46,233 --> 00:29:49,067
Go. Go to bed, okay?

637
00:29:49,067 --> 00:29:50,533
- Okay, fine.
- Good night.

638
00:29:50,533 --> 00:29:52,900
Are you going to think of him
while trying to sleep?

639
00:29:52,900 --> 00:29:55,167
- Stop it. Good night!
- Good night!

640
00:29:55,167 --> 00:30:02,167
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

641
00:30:06,167 --> 00:30:08,400
[RUDY] Yes, Gabo and I talked.

642
00:30:09,100 --> 00:30:12,167
He promised
he'd turn over a new leaf.

643
00:30:12,300 --> 00:30:13,733
[BONG] Wow.

644
00:30:13,867 --> 00:30:15,100
Is that true, Gabo?

645
00:30:16,033 --> 00:30:18,333
A while ago, you said
you were going to behave.

646
00:30:18,467 --> 00:30:20,700
You went inside, you came
back out, and attacked Django.

647
00:30:20,833 --> 00:30:22,500
[LAUGHTER]

648
00:30:22,633 --> 00:30:24,867
[IPE] C'mon, Gabo,
we know you very well,

649
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:27,867
so I am sure
that will never happen!

650
00:30:28,100 --> 00:30:29,733
You guys are
so hard on Gabo!

651
00:30:29,867 --> 00:30:31,967
Why don't we try
trusting our friend?

652
00:30:32,100 --> 00:30:34,967
Who knows, maybe this time
it's for real, right?

653
00:30:35,100 --> 00:30:36,633
- We really hope so.
- We really hope so.

654
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:38,700
- [CHUCKLING]
- It's real this time.

655
00:30:40,867 --> 00:30:42,333
I already promised Papa.

656
00:30:43,633 --> 00:30:45,033
I told him that...

657
00:30:45,167 --> 00:30:46,700
I'm really going
to turn over a new leaf.

658
00:30:47,600 --> 00:30:48,867
I've been thinking...

659
00:30:49,733 --> 00:30:51,800
I spent a long time in prison,

660
00:30:53,433 --> 00:30:55,333
and if I just waste my life,

661
00:30:55,467 --> 00:30:56,633
nothing will come of it.

662
00:30:57,400 --> 00:30:58,800
Do you believe me now?

663
00:30:58,933 --> 00:31:00,300
- [BETCHAY] Hmm.
- Alright.

664
00:31:00,433 --> 00:31:03,100
- Take a shot.
- Your father is right, Gabo.

665
00:31:03,633 --> 00:31:06,000
- [COUGHS]
- Don't stoop to their level.

666
00:31:06,133 --> 00:31:08,500
Their lives are already
ruined anyway,

667
00:31:08,633 --> 00:31:12,233
that's why they do things
that harm others.

668
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:16,667
[MAMENG] And don't let your
temper get the better of you.

669
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:23,167
It might just end up ruining
your life and your future.

670
00:31:23,300 --> 00:31:24,967
Those people are just looking

671
00:31:25,100 --> 00:31:26,567
for someone
to drag down with them.

672
00:31:26,700 --> 00:31:27,833
[IPE] They're back Gabo.

673
00:31:28,533 --> 00:31:31,167
To be honest, you don't
have to prove them anything.

674
00:31:31,300 --> 00:31:35,100
Everyone around here knows
that Django is no match for you

675
00:31:35,233 --> 00:31:37,033
That's why he wants
to get back at you, right?

676
00:31:37,167 --> 00:31:38,733
Yeah, but the problem is

677
00:31:38,867 --> 00:31:41,033
when they both get involved...

678
00:31:41,300 --> 00:31:43,333
- I'll get mad.
- [LAUGHTER]

679
00:31:43,500 --> 00:31:45,700
Oh, Rudy, your son?

680
00:31:45,833 --> 00:31:47,567
He won't be able to hold back!

681
00:31:47,700 --> 00:31:50,467
He's always looking for a fight!

682
00:31:50,600 --> 00:31:52,533
As soon as he gets
out in the streets...

683
00:31:52,667 --> 00:31:54,933
- kapow!
- [LAUGHTER]

684
00:31:55,067 --> 00:31:56,267
Don't encourage him!

685
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:58,100
- Enough.
- [MAMENG] Wait a minute!

686
00:31:58,533 --> 00:32:01,633
Why are you always
against Gabo?

687
00:32:01,933 --> 00:32:04,467
- You started it!
- Let's cheers to that.

688
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:06,467
- [LAUGHTER]
- [TEKLA] Stop it.

689
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:08,200
Aunt Betchay.

690
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:10,833
In my conversation
with my father,

691
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:12,667
I really told him

692
00:32:13,267 --> 00:32:14,467
that I'm turning over
a new leaf,

693
00:32:15,067 --> 00:32:16,267
so tomorrow...

694
00:32:16,833 --> 00:32:18,367
I'll look for a job.

695
00:32:19,033 --> 00:32:20,567
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

696
00:32:20,700 --> 00:32:22,067
Hey, man.

697
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:24,533
- Hey.
- Do you repair motorcycles?

698
00:32:24,867 --> 00:32:26,800
Yes, we do!

699
00:32:26,933 --> 00:32:28,200
Do you need yours fixed?

700
00:32:28,333 --> 00:32:31,400
Yes, the side of my motorcycle
got damaged.

701
00:32:31,533 --> 00:32:34,033
Bring it here tomorrow
so we can see it.

702
00:32:34,167 --> 00:32:35,700
How much do you think
it will cost?

703
00:32:35,833 --> 00:32:37,900
- Just the sides, right?
- Yes, just the sides.

704
00:32:38,533 --> 00:32:40,100
It might be around two thousand.

705
00:32:41,367 --> 00:32:43,400
[BETCHAY] He'll look for a job!

706
00:32:43,533 --> 00:32:45,700
Really? Thank goodness

707
00:32:45,833 --> 00:32:48,567
you won't go around
fighting anymore!

708
00:32:48,700 --> 00:32:51,000
[CHUCKLING]

709
00:32:51,167 --> 00:32:52,600
Hey, you guys.

710
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:55,167
If you want,

711
00:32:55,733 --> 00:32:57,067
you can join me in looking
for a job tomorrow

712
00:32:57,200 --> 00:32:58,133
- Sure!
- Yeah!

713
00:32:58,267 --> 00:33:00,400
We'll definitely go
with you to earn money.

714
00:33:00,533 --> 00:33:01,833
- We're your plus ones!
- [TEKLA] You're right.

715
00:33:01,967 --> 00:33:03,133
Hey, this is perfect!

716
00:33:03,267 --> 00:33:05,133
We're actually being kicked
out of the house.

717
00:33:05,267 --> 00:33:07,533
They even had the nerve
to call us useless.

718
00:33:07,667 --> 00:33:08,700
[LAUGHTER]

719
00:33:08,833 --> 00:33:10,667
[RUDY] You should tell them
that they're right!

720
00:33:10,800 --> 00:33:12,567
[TEKLA] That's right. Cheers!

721
00:33:12,700 --> 00:33:14,533
- [LAUGHTER]
- They're right!

722
00:33:14,667 --> 00:33:17,367
I was just joking! C'mon!

723
00:33:19,867 --> 00:33:23,800
Someone's interested in
the motorcycle you're fixing.

724
00:33:23,967 --> 00:33:24,933
He wants to buy it.

725
00:33:25,067 --> 00:33:27,400
What? But it's not for sale.

726
00:33:27,700 --> 00:33:30,300
Yeah, but... why don't you
talk to him instead?

727
00:33:30,433 --> 00:33:32,333
- [MAMENG] Who is it?
- Wait a minute.

728
00:33:32,467 --> 00:33:34,000
- Who is it?
- He's buying it?

729
00:33:34,133 --> 00:33:35,933
- Hey, grab a drink with us!
- Take a shot with us!

730
00:33:37,100 --> 00:33:39,167
I can't it's against
my religion.

731
00:33:39,300 --> 00:33:40,733
[BONG] His religion? What is it?

732
00:33:40,867 --> 00:33:43,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

733
00:33:43,833 --> 00:33:47,800
This is Rudy, he assembles
all the motorcycles here.

734
00:33:48,367 --> 00:33:49,733
Is that customized, sir?

735
00:33:49,867 --> 00:33:52,600
[ELTON] It is. He assembled it
on his own.

736
00:33:52,733 --> 00:33:55,533
The owner of it is a seaman.
He just hasn't gone back to it.

737
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:58,033
Is that so? How much do those
usually cost, sir?

738
00:33:58,167 --> 00:34:02,200
[RUDY] Oh, it usually could go
up to 300,000 pesos.

739
00:34:02,433 --> 00:34:03,600
It's quite expensive, huh.

740
00:34:04,533 --> 00:34:07,400
- It's as expensive as a car.
- But well, look at it!

741
00:34:07,533 --> 00:34:09,500
- It's real sleek.
- Mm-hmm. It's stunning.

742
00:34:09,633 --> 00:34:11,500
[RUDY] You can consider it
as an artwork.

743
00:34:11,633 --> 00:34:13,067
[ELTON] Its wheels alone
is already gorgeous.

744
00:34:13,200 --> 00:34:14,167
[RUDY] Mm-hmm.

745
00:34:14,300 --> 00:34:15,500
[ELTON] It already looks good.

746
00:34:15,633 --> 00:34:19,033
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

747
00:34:19,167 --> 00:34:20,267
Well then, sir.

748
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:22,467
- I'll come back tomorrow.
- Sure. We'll wait for you.

749
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:24,467
[RUDY] You should customize
yours, too!

750
00:34:25,133 --> 00:34:26,200
[ELTON] Yeah.

751
00:34:26,700 --> 00:34:27,733
- [MAMENG LAUGHING]
- [TEKLA] Oh, dear...

752
00:34:27,867 --> 00:34:29,500
- [IPE] There he goes.
- [MAMENG WHEEZING, COUGHS]

753
00:34:29,667 --> 00:34:31,600
[MAMENG] What? Did they strike
a deal?

754
00:34:33,567 --> 00:34:34,700
[BONG] Gabo!

755
00:34:35,733 --> 00:34:38,133
- [BONG] You good?
- [MAMENG] Are you alright?

756
00:34:40,633 --> 00:34:41,833
That man was glaring at me.

757
00:34:41,967 --> 00:34:43,400
Why? Who was it?

758
00:34:43,900 --> 00:34:46,200
I recognize his face but I can't
remember who he is.

759
00:34:46,333 --> 00:34:47,533
Maybe he offended you before!

760
00:34:47,667 --> 00:34:49,233
- That bastard!
- Hey! Hey! Hey!

761
00:34:49,367 --> 00:34:52,367
- Hold it!
- Stop right there! Hey!

762
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:55,333
Hey! What's up with him?
Who's he after?

763
00:34:55,467 --> 00:34:58,667
I thought he'll change but now
he's causing trouble again!

764
00:34:58,800 --> 00:35:02,100
Why would they go after him
he's just buying a motorcycle?

765
00:35:07,767 --> 00:35:08,967
[BONG] Hey!

766
00:35:09,767 --> 00:35:10,867
Hey!

767
00:35:14,933 --> 00:35:16,467
Come on. Let's go to Gabo!

768
00:35:18,367 --> 00:35:20,133
- [BONG] Gabo!
- [TEKLA] Oh, they're here.

769
00:35:20,267 --> 00:35:21,500
We couldn't catch him.

770
00:35:21,633 --> 00:35:23,300
- Why?
- He's quite quick.

771
00:35:23,433 --> 00:35:24,667
I thought you said
he's just a turtle to you.

772
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:26,267
- Man, was he quick.
- [LAUGHTER]

773
00:35:26,400 --> 00:35:27,567
Turns out you were the turtles!

774
00:35:27,700 --> 00:35:30,267
- [LAUGHTER]
- So it were you guys.

775
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:32,400
Stop standing around
and clean this up!

776
00:35:32,533 --> 00:35:34,400
- Come on, let's tidy up.
- You frauds!

777
00:35:34,533 --> 00:35:35,733
- I got it.
- This one's not finished yet.

778
00:35:35,900 --> 00:35:37,300
[ELTON] Alright, pack it up!

779
00:35:37,433 --> 00:35:40,167
- [RUDY] Go home already!
- [ELTON] I'll go home now.

780
00:35:40,700 --> 00:35:42,667
- [BONG] Come on.
- [RUDY] You should get going.

781
00:35:42,800 --> 00:35:43,800
- [BONG] Bye, Sir Rudy!
- [RUDY] Be careful!

782
00:35:43,933 --> 00:35:44,967
- [BONG] Thanks, Gabo!
- [RUDY] Yeah!

783
00:35:45,100 --> 00:35:46,233
[TEKLA] Good night!

784
00:35:46,367 --> 00:35:48,500
- I'll get going. Take care.
- See you tomorrow!

785
00:35:48,633 --> 00:35:55,567
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

786
00:35:57,167 --> 00:35:58,600
[WATER SPLASHES]

787
00:35:59,100 --> 00:36:00,533
[ELECTRIC BUZZING]

788
00:36:00,667 --> 00:36:04,833
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

789
00:36:10,067 --> 00:36:17,033
[GABO SCREAMING, GROANING
IN PAIN]

790
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:33,333
<i>I do hope you really change
for the better.</i>

791
00:36:33,467 --> 00:36:35,867
Don't worry, Pa. I'll see to it
<i> that once we come back here,</i>

792
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:37,267
<i> we already have jobs.</i>

793
00:36:38,767 --> 00:36:40,200
Your son, Gabo, is really kind.

794
00:36:40,333 --> 00:36:43,100
<i> He's just really unfortunate.</i>

795
00:36:43,267 --> 00:36:44,367
<i> Get yours now!</i>

796
00:36:44,500 --> 00:36:45,567
<i> What? We look like thugs?</i>

797
00:36:45,700 --> 00:36:46,767
<i> Come here yourself then!</i>

798
00:36:46,900 --> 00:36:47,967
<i>I don't think these punks
know who we are!</i>

799
00:36:48,100 --> 00:36:49,633
<i>You're brave hiding behind
your screens, huh?!</i>

800
00:36:49,767 --> 00:36:50,933
[CRASHES]

801
00:36:51,067 --> 00:36:54,067
[MALE VO] Whoever goes against
the people of Ginintuang Lupa...

802
00:36:54,200 --> 00:36:55,567
<i> I own this land!</i>

803
00:36:55,700 --> 00:36:57,600
[MALE VO] is sure to fall.

804
00:36:57,733 --> 00:36:58,800
<i> Ricardo!</i>

805
00:36:58,933 --> 00:37:04,300
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [BOTH GRUNTING]

806
00:37:04,433 --> 00:37:05,400
[THUDS]

807
00:37:05,533 --> 00:37:08,533
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

808
00:37:08,667 --> 00:37:11,933
[MALE VO] It's time to show off
this Thursday.

809
00:37:13,267 --> 00:37:15,133
[MALE VO] Coco Martin's Sigabo.
